  "source": "The Swedish National Court Administration",
  "note": [
    "The table illustrates the performance of the time targets at the district courts set by the government, measured in months at the 75th percentile for cases determined during the selected time period (time from filed case to determined case).",
    "The target for Criminal cases excluding priority cases is 5 months and the target for Civil cases excluding joint petitions for divorce is 7 months.",
    "Priority cases are criminal cases involving a detained person or a defendant under 18 years of age, these cases shall be handled promptly. Cases and matters at the Patent and Market Court (a part of Stockholm District Court) are also excluded."
  ]
